# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in real values. Never commit secrets.
#
# Multi-key convention
# --------------------
# A provider may have up to nine keys. The first is `PROVIDER_API_KEY`; extras are
# `PROVIDER_API_KEY_2` ... `PROVIDER_API_KEY_9`. Keys are tried in ascending order,
# and the gateway fails over to the next key only when the earlier key is rejected
# (401/403) or rate-limited (429). Extra keys spread traffic and survive a revoked
# key; they do NOT raise the provider's account-level quota.
#
# Supported providers: GROQ, NVIDIA, OLLAMA (and any OpenAI-compatible provider the
# engine is configured with, using the same `<PROVIDER>_API_KEY` pattern).

# --- Web client (publishable values only; exposed to the browser) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxx

# --- Groq (chat + chart insight in dev) ---
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxx
# GROQ_API_KEY_2=gsk_xxx
# GROQ_API_KEY_3=gsk_xxx

# --- NVIDIA NIM (secondary chat/reasoning provider) ---
NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-xxx
# NVIDIA_API_KEY_2=nvapi-xxx

# --- Ollama (local or hosted; key optional when running a local daemon) ---
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=xxx
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434

# --- Engine / server-side only (never expose to the browser) ---
# IREME_REPORTS_DB=./var/ireme-reports.sqlite3
# IREME_ARTIFACTS_DIR=./var/artifacts
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=xxx
